# Development Workflow

## Quick Reference

```bash
make build                                                     # Build all crates
make release                                                   # Build the distributable app and embedded runtime
make test                                                      # Run all tests with one pinned embedded server
cargo run -p u-forge                                           # Run the desktop app
```

Bundled SQLite compiles with a standard C compiler on `PATH`. Environment
variables are optional overrides; see
[environment-config.mdc](mdc:.rulesdir/environment-config.mdc).

---

## First Time Setup

1. Install Rust stable ([rustup.rs](https://rustup.rs)), a C compiler (`gcc`,
   `clang`, or MSVC), and the platform GPUI libraries listed in `BUILD.md`.
2. `make build` — the first x86_64 Linux GNU build also downloads the pinned
   upstream Ubuntu x64 Embeddable Lemonade artifact. Set
   `UFORGE_SKIP_EMBEDDED_LEMONADE=1` to skip automatic provisioning; without an
   existing artifact the app stays graph-only.
3. Optionally install a standalone
   [Lemonade Server](https://github.com/lemonade-sdk/lemonade) when developing
   against an externally managed service.
4. `make test` — provisions and owns one checksum-pinned embedded server for
   the complete suite, then tears down its process tree. No external server or
   environment configuration is required.
5. `cargo run -p u-forge` — launch the desktop app.

